MAJORITY ELEMENT – II (Elements Appearing More Than ⌊n/3⌋ Times)

👉 You already solved Majority Element (n/2)
👉 This n/3 version is harder and frequently asked in product-based interviews

1️⃣ Problem Statement

Given an integer array nums, return all elements that appear more than ⌊n/3⌋ times.

At most 2 elements can satisfy this condition.

Example 1
Input: nums = [3,2,3]
Output: [3]

Example 2
Input: nums = [1,1,1,3,3,2,2,2]
Output: [1,2]

2️⃣ Key Observation 💡 (VERY IMPORTANT)

For n/3, there can be at most two majority elements

Uses extended Moore’s Voting Algorithm

3️⃣ Algorithm (Two-Pass Approach)
Pass 1: Find Candidates

Maintain:

candidate1, candidate2

count1, count2

Pass 2: Verify

Count actual frequency of candidates

Include only if count > ⌊n/3⌋

4️⃣ Algorithm Steps
➤ First Pass

If number equals candidate1 → count1++

Else if equals candidate2 → count2++

Else if count1 == 0 → set candidate1

Else if count2 == 0 → set candidate2

Else → decrement both counts

➤ Second Pass

Re-count frequency

Confirm valid majorities

5️⃣ Java Code (Clean & Interview-Ready)
import java.util.*;

class MajorityElementII {

    public static List<Integer> majorityElement(int[] nums) {

        int candidate1 = 0, candidate2 = 0;
        int count1 = 0, count2 = 0;

        // First pass: find candidates
        for (int num : nums) {
            if (candidate1 == num) {
                count1++;
            } else if (candidate2 == num) {
                count2++;
            } else if (count1 == 0) {
                candidate1 = num;
                count1 = 1;
            } else if (count2 == 0) {
                candidate2 = num;
                count2 = 1;
            } else {
                count1--;
                count2--;
            }
        }

        // Second pass: verify candidates
        count1 = 0;
        count2 = 0;

        for (int num : nums) {
            if (num == candidate1) count1++;
            else if (num == candidate2) count2++;
        }

        List<Integer> result = new ArrayList<>();
        int n = nums.length;

        if (count1 > n / 3) result.add(candidate1);
        if (count2 > n / 3) result.add(candidate2);

        return result;
    }
}

